 `request` and `response` can be `null` for deliveries that have not started yet or are still in progress. The delivery request headers omit the `X-Webhook-Signature` header.
+
+## Delivery behavior
+
+Fizzy sends a POST to a webhook's payload URL when a subscribed board event occurs. Each event is delivered once per active webhook. Requests are signed with HMAC-SHA256 using the webhook's signing secret.
+
+A delivery is recorded as failed for a non-2XX HTTP response or a connection error. Ten consecutive failures within one hour deactivate the webhook. Deactivated webhooks can be reactivated from the webhook page; reactivation resets the failure counter.
+
+Delivery history is retained for one week and removed automatically every 15 minutes.
diff --git a/test/models/webhook/delivery_http_test.rb b/test/models/webhook/delivery_http_test.rb
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..642e289
--- /dev/null
+++ b/test/models/webhook/delivery_http_test.rb
@@ -0,0 +1,54 @@
+require "test_helper"
+
+class Webhook::DeliveryHttpTest < ActiveSupport::TestCase
+  test "posts signed json and records a successful delivery exactly once" do
+    webhook = webhooks(:active)
+    event = events(:text_published)
+
+    stub_request(:post, webhook.url).to_return(status: 204, body: "")
+
+    delivery = Webhook::Delivery.create!(webhook: webhook, event: event)
+
+    assert_difference "Webhook::Delivery.count", 0 do
+      2.times { delivery.deliver_now }
+    end
+
+    assert_requested :post, webhook.url, times: 1
+    assert delivery.reload.completed?
+    assert delivery.succeeded?
+
+    request_headers = delivery.request.dig("headers")
+    assert_equal "fizzy/1.0.0 Webhook", request_headers["User-Agent"]
+    assert_equal "application/json", request_headers["Content-Type"]
+    assert request_headers["X-Webhook-Signature"].present?
+    assert request_headers["X-Webhook-Timestamp"].present?
+  end
+
+  test "records a non-2xx response as failed" do
+    webhook = webhooks(:active)
+    event = events(:layout_commented)
+
+    stub_request(:post, webhook.url).to_return(status: 422, body: "")
+
+    delivery = Webhook::Delivery.create!(webhook: webhook, event: event)
+    delivery.deliver_now
+
+    assert_requested :post, webhook.url, times: 1
+    assert delivery.reload.completed?
+    assert_not delivery.succeeded?
+    assert_equal 422, delivery.response["code"]
+  end
+
+  test "inactive webhook does not deliver queued work" do
+    webhook = webhooks(:inactive)
+    event = events(:layout_commented)
+
+    stub_request(:post, webhook.url).to_return(status: 204, body: "")
+
+    delivery = Webhook::Delivery.create!(webhook: webhook, event: event)
+    delivery.deliver_now
+
+    assert_not_requested :post, webhook.url
+    assert delivery.reload.pending?
+  end
+end
